       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there is a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily. This is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for depression, and for most anxiety disorders.\n- **25 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for panic disorder, PTSD, and some older or sensitive patients.\n- **200 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the maximum dose.\n\nIf 1000 mg is intended, please confirm that and tell me the clinical rationale. I would also want to add a note to the order for pharmacist review. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
